Scanning electron microscopy (SEM) study shows the as-synthesized MOF precursor exhibited an orthorhombic morphology with the long-edge length of 5 to \(7\,\upmu\mathrm{m}\) (Figure 1a). The Fe-free Cd-MOF exhibited similar morphologies to those of the Fe-containing Cd-MOF, suggesting there was no change in the type of MOF structure after the addition of Fe (Figure S1). The SEM image of the as-synthesized catalyst revealed the MOF crystals transformed into irregular shapes after the pyrolysis (Figure 1b). Powder X-ray diffraction (PXRD) pattern shows two broad peaks for the Fe-C-N750 catalyst (Figure 1c). The broad peak centered around \(25^{\circ}\ 2\theta\) is mainly from the carbonaceous matrices. The peak centered near \(43^{\circ}\,2\theta\) could be assigned to the (101) plane of the 2H phase graphite.

